/**
 * Offline service worker: after the first visit, Boids never touches the
 * network again, and never updates.
 *
 * First visit: download every file of the app (FILES, generated by
 * `npm run build` with the SHA-256 of each file's content) into the device's
 * cache, check each against its hash, and save them all or nothing. This is
 * the only time the app is downloaded.
 *
 * From then on, every request the app makes is answered from that saved
 * copy. Nothing is ever fetched: a request for anything not saved gets an
 * error, never the network.
 *
 * Zero updates: the version saved first is frozen. When a browser finds a
 * different sw.js (browsers re-check it when an installed web app opens
 * online, and a web page cannot switch that off), the new worker refuses to
 * install before downloading a single file, so the frozen version keeps
 * running. The one exception is moving a device off an earlier, updating
 * build of Boids, which used the network: that happens once and then this
 * version is frozen too.
 *
 * Activation deletes only this app's other caches, so other apps on the same
 * origin (e.g. other GitHub Pages projects) keep theirs.
 */

